From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Lezhankin <abyss.7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 14:05:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] openvpn: support certificates on smart cards (PKCS#11)

Add the "pkcs11" connection type of NetworkManager-openvpn (see
NetworkManager-openvpn!108): the certificate and key are referenced by a
PKCS#11 ID (--pkcs11-id) and the smart card PIN is the cert-pass secret.

The Detect button lists the certificates of the plugged in tokens with
"openvpn --show-pkcs11-ids" through the p11-kit proxy module.

The PIN is always masked in the password dialog, even when the prompt
mentions a "token".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
